{"id":"3459ca75da2e14a7","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-monochar.md","title":"Positive DNF characterization","display":"thm-monochar — Positive DNF characterization","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-monochar","aliases":["27-thm-monochar"],"display":"thm-monochar — Positive DNF characterization","depends_on":["[[27-df-monotone]]","[[27-df-monodnf]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-monochar"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-monochar</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-monochar — Positive DNF characterization"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"814b17f1550bcf38\" href=\"?note=814b17f1550bcf38\" title=\"27-df-monodnf\">27-df-monodnf</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\">\\([n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\\)</span>, as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5d10aed668d85817\" href=\"?note=5d10aed668d85817\" title=\"27-df-boolfunc\">27-df-boolfunc</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DNF}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\)</span> are as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0b618255959ff4bc\" href=\"?note=0b618255959ff4bc\" title=\"27-df-dnf\">27-df-dnf</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MonotoneDNF}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{MonotoneDNF}_n\\)</span> denote the positive classes defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"814b17f1550bcf38\" href=\"?note=814b17f1550bcf38\" title=\"27-df-monodnf\">27-df-monodnf</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\exists D\\in\\mathrm{MonotoneDNF}_n\\;(f=\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D))\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\exists D\\in\\mathrm{MonotoneDNF}_n\\;(f=\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D))\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Crama–Hammer (2011), §1.10.2, Theorem 1.21 and its corollary，印刷页 36，PDF 第 60 页（从 1 计数）。 已核对证明：正函数的负文字可从素蕴涵项中删除；反向全正文字项的析取保持递增。原书术语是 positive，而不是允许不同变量取不同极性的 monotone。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-monotone","status":"resolved","id":"640eb8f2fbffd9d9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","exc